  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Political Economy Analysis of the Mining Sector in Zambia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p&gt;In-depth research on the most significant risks and opportunities that are associated with the governance of the Zambia&apos;s extractive sector of critical raw materials  and its value chain. This task will be completed through a Political Economy Analysis (PEA) and will have three specific objectives: &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;1.Identify the formal and informal factors of the Zambian political settlement that affect the mining sector. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;2.Identify potential priorities and opportunities  for governance interventions developed by the EU and EU member states in the Zambia&apos;s mining sector. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;3.Provide contextual elements for the identification and prioritization of activities under the sustainable raw materials value chains roadmap. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</narrative>
  </description>
